From: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ask2(T-M6-T3): add the 3-tuple coarse-flow CC key packer

Adds cc_pack_key_3tuple() and CC_KEY_SIZE_3TUPLE (10 bytes: PORT_ID +
SIP + DIP + PROTO, no L4 ports), the leaf-level building block for
T-M6-T3 (plans/ASK2-MASTER-PLAN.md 4.6 M6-F). Byte layout is
silicon-confirmed, not guessed: live-read on `.106` (the vendor ASK
1.x oracle) of KeyGen scheme 6 (ekfc=0x801c0000 =
PORT_ID|IPSRC1|IPDST1|PTYPE1, the vendor's own tuple3udp4/tcp4_cc
scheme) via bin/kg-scheme-read.py + bin/fman-full-capture.py
--follow-rccb: CCOBASE=5 -> FMBM_RCCB+0x50, group-table row w0 =
0x4a20ff08 -> keysize field = 10, matching PORT_ID(1)+SIP(4)+DIP(4)+
PROTO(1) exactly, no truncation or padding gap. PORT_ID is byte 0,
deterministically 0x00 on this ucode (same finding this project
already established for cc_pack_key_dual_pid()).

Scope, deliberately bounded: this is the packer + KUnit pin only,
mirroring how cc_pack_key_dual() itself was introduced before its
later dual_lane/dual_lane_pid dispatch wiring (0185). Marked
__maybe_unused so it compiles clean under -Werror before any caller
exists. NOT wired into fman_pcd_cc_static_install()'s spec/hw
dispatch, NOT armed via any KeyGen scheme-attach path, NOT reachable
from ask.ko. Per the master plan's own binding rule ("never implement
a coarse flow by truncating a full extracted key -- keysize MUST
equal the extraction length, add only for explicit kernel wildcard
flow semantics"), wiring this into ask_flow_offload.c's tc-flower
dispatch (the natural entry point, matching how the existing 0198
tc-flower hook already handles non-flowtable-sourced hardware rules)
is separate follow-on work, not attempted blind here.

v2: fixed two malformed-diff bugs in the original hunk headers
(wrong old/new line counts, and blank context lines missing their
required leading space) that made the first CI run fall back to a
partial/fuzzy `patch -p1` apply -- the #include hunk silently never
applied, so fman_pcd_cc_3tuple_key never got compiled/registered as
a KUnit suite (confirmed on .185: dmesg showed "1..2" suites, not
the expected 3). Headers below are now programmatically verified
against the actual hunk bodies, not hand-counted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GooC2zFmzRBYLikPbwekuH
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c
@@ -595,8 +595,66 @@
 	row = (u8 __force *)match + (size_t)idx * 2 * CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL_PID;
 	memcpy_toio((void __iomem *)row, key, CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL_PID);
 	memcpy_toio((void __iomem *)(row + CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL_PID), msk, CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL_PID);
 }
 
+#define CC_KEY_SIZE_3TUPLE	10U
+
+/*
+ * T-M6-T3 3-tuple coarse-flow key: PORT_ID + SIP + DIP + PROTO, no ports.
+ * Board-confirmed byte-exact against the vendor's own tuple3 KeyGen scheme
+ * on .106 (EKFC 0x801c0000 = PORT_ID|IPSRC1|IPDST1|PTYPE1; live scheme 6
+ * group-table row keysize field = 10, matching this layout with no
+ * truncation or padding gap -- see the changelog entry for the exact
+ * register readback). PORT_ID is byte 0, deterministically 0x00 on this
+ * ucode (same finding as cc_pack_key_dual_pid() above). IPv4 only -- the
+ * vendor scheme this mirrors has no IPv6 lane.
+ *
+ * MUST NOT be reached by any full 5-tuple flow: this key type exists only
+ * for explicit kernel wildcard/coarse-flow semantics (no L4 ports
+ * present), per plans/ASK2-MASTER-PLAN.md T-M6-T3. Truncating a real
+ * 5-tuple key down to this width would silently merge distinct flows --
+ * whatever caller eventually wires this in MUST gate on the kernel's own
+ * wildcard intent, not on this function's field-presence checks (which
+ * only decide which of the present fields get written, not whether coarse
+ * matching was actually requested).
+ *
+ * __maybe_unused: not yet wired into fman_pcd_cc_static_install()'s
+ * spec/hw dispatch or any KeyGen scheme-attach path -- this is the
+ * packer primitive only (mirrors how cc_pack_key_dual() itself started
+ * before 0185's dual_lane/dual_lane_pid dispatch wiring). Pinned by
+ * tests/fman_pcd_cc_3tuple_key_test.c.
+ */
+static void __maybe_unused cc_pack_key_3tuple(void __iomem *match, u16 idx,
+					      const struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_key *k)
+{
+	u8 key[CC_KEY_SIZE_3TUPLE];
+	u8 msk[CC_KEY_SIZE_3TUPLE];
+	u8 *row;
+
+	memset(key, 0, sizeof(key));
+	memset(msk, 0, sizeof(msk));
+
+	/* byte 0: PORT_ID, deterministically 0x00 on this ucode. */
+	msk[0] = 0xff;
+
+	if (k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_SRC_IP) {
+		memcpy(&key[1], &k->src_ip_be, 4);
+		msk[1] = msk[2] = msk[3] = msk[4] = 0xff;
+	}
+	if (k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_DST_IP) {
+		memcpy(&key[5], &k->dst_ip_be, 4);
+		msk[5] = msk[6] = msk[7] = msk[8] = 0xff;
+	}
+	if (k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_PROTO) {
+		key[9] = k->proto;
+		msk[9] = 0xff;
+	}
+
+	row = (u8 __force *)match + (size_t)idx * 2 * CC_KEY_SIZE_3TUPLE;
+	memcpy_toio((void __iomem *)row, key, CC_KEY_SIZE_3TUPLE);
+	memcpy_toio((void __iomem *)(row + CC_KEY_SIZE_3TUPLE), msk, CC_KEY_SIZE_3TUPLE);
+}
+
 /*
  * Encode one leaf (result) action descriptor at AD row @idx - SDK-convergent
  * RESULT AD (0115; SDK FillAdOfTypeResult, sdk_fm_cc.c:2227-2343).
@@ -859,5 +908,6 @@
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fman_pcd_cc_static_get_base);
 
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_FSL_FMAN_PCD_KUNIT_TEST)
 #include "tests/fman_pcd_cc_dual_key_test.c"
+#include "tests/fman_pcd_cc_3tuple_key_test.c"
 #endif /* CONFIG_FSL_FMAN_PCD_KUNIT_TEST */
